      Question
  xFusionCorp Industries is planning to host two static websites on their infra in Stratos Datacenter. The development of these websites is still in-progress, but we want to get the servers ready. Please perform the following steps to accomplish the task:

 1-Install httpd package and dependencies on app server 3.
 2-Apache should serve on port 6400.
 3-There are two website's backups /home/thor/official and /home/thor/games on jump_host. Set them up on Apache in a way that official should work on the link http://localhost:6400/official/ and games should work on link http://localhost:6400/games/ on the mentioned app server.
 4-Once configured you should be able to access the website using curl command on the respective app server, i.e curl http://localhost:6400/official/ and curl http://localhost:6400/games/

   Solution
 1- Login into app server 3
     ssh banner@stapp03
  - Install http, enable and start it
     sudo yum install -y httpd
     sudo systemctl enable httpd
     sudo systemctl start httpd
 2- Change Apache port
     sudo cp /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf.bak
     sudo sed -i 's/80/6400/g' /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf
  - Restart httpd
     sudo systemctl restart httpd
 3- Copy backup from Kumphost to App Server
  - Login into JumpHost
     ssh thor@jump_host
  - Copy backup
     scp -r /home/thor/official banner@stapp03:/home/banner
     scp -r /home/thor/games banner@stapp03:/home/banner/
 4- Place Websites
  - Login into App Server 3
     ssh banner@stapp03
  - Place into Website
     sudo cp -r /home/banner/official /var/www/html/
     sudo cp -r /home/banner/games /var/www/html
  - Restart httpd
     sudo systemctl restart httpd
  - Verify result
     curl http://localhost:6400/games/
     curl http://localhost:6400/official/
